I know this has been mentioned before, but I say it again (after a frustrating
situation in a game yesterday).  There should be a command to "shove" some-
thing.  Regarding monsters/pets, it would be helpful, if when in a doorway 
with 3 monsters attacking and your pet in the corrodor trying to get in on
the action, to be able to "shove" your pet away and back up into the hallway,
so only one monster at a time can attack.  Also, it would be humorous and
helpful, to be able to shove monsters into previously identified traps:
	The orc hits!
	"s"hove
	In what direction?
	You shove the orc into the teleportation trap.--more--
	The orc disappears.

"k"ick does not work this way, and I wouldn't want to "k"ick Mittens (my cat),
thus doing damage to it.

It would also be nice, when running away from a nasty and that helpful pre-
viously identified trap door is ahead of you, to be able to shove your pet onto
the trap door, before diving into it yourself, thus saving poor old Mittens
from forgetfulness if it takes a while to return to that level.

Of course, "s"hove would depend on your strength: stronger characters could 
shove an object/monster more than one space away.  Also, shoving a grid bug
would be no problem, shoving a troll might require a minimum strength, shoving
a mumak or a dragon...well, maybe not at all.
	The red dragon hits!  The red dragon claws!--more--
	The red dragon hits!
	"s"hove
	You are unable to move the red dragon.
	The red dragon hits (as it chuckles at your attempt)...

But, in order to keep things halfway fair, the monster should be allowed to
get its hit(s) it first before the effect of the shove...or else there could
be massive abuse of the command.

But, we don't want to make this game too easy.  :-)

Just my $0.02.

